1
00:00:07,520 --> 00:00:08,920
SAY NO TO PIRACY, SUPPORT ORIGINALS

2
00:02:03,840 --> 00:02:05,400
After that day,

3
00:02:05,920 --> 00:02:08,560
it feels like Luan Nian
has put a spell on me.

4
00:02:09,320 --> 00:02:11,520
He unlocked the secret of my desire.

5
00:02:15,400 --> 00:02:16,720
Did you notice?

6
00:02:17,400 --> 00:02:19,000
You cannot control the feelings of love.

7
00:02:20,080 --> 00:02:22,320
And all those years,
he made me long for more.

8
00:02:22,400 --> 00:02:23,960
He drove me crazy and lived in my mind.

9
00:02:24,880 --> 00:02:27,320
Shang Zhitao, are you sober?

10
00:02:28,520 --> 00:02:30,480
Do you understand what's
going to happen next?

11
00:02:30,560 --> 00:02:32,880
I spent six years

12
00:02:33,480 --> 00:02:36,160
in this shameful, hidden relationship.

13
00:02:37,120 --> 00:02:39,600
There were grievances, pain,

14
00:02:40,680 --> 00:02:42,480
and joy.

15
00:02:43,720 --> 00:02:48,280
Yet I can never take the
first step to leave him.

16
00:02:51,120 --> 00:02:55,720
ADAPTED FROM THE EARLY SPRING ON
JJWXC.NET AUTHOR: GU NIANG BIE KU

17
00:02:58,120 --> 00:03:01,600
"YOU ARE NOT SUITABLE"

18
00:04:17,070 --> 00:04:18,680
The interview is about to begin, Luke.

19
00:04:19,640 --> 00:04:21,320
Shang Zhitao.

20
00:04:22,120 --> 00:04:24,920
Hi. I am Liang Xin, Lime's HR manager.

21
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:26,400
You can call me Tracy.

22
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:29,080
Today, your chief interviewer is Luke Luan.

23
00:04:29,680 --> 00:04:32,200
If you're ready, let's begin.

24
00:04:33,080 --> 00:04:34,120
Okay.

25
00:04:35,440 --> 00:04:36,720
I am Shang Zhitao.

26
00:04:36,800 --> 00:04:38,120
My English name is Flora.

27
00:04:38,200 --> 00:04:41,120
I am from Harbin, and I
attended university in Nanjing.

28
00:04:41,200 --> 00:04:42,440
I'm a fresh graduate.

29
00:04:42,520 --> 00:04:44,920
I would love to work at Lime.

30
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:46,960
Tell me about your work experience.

31
00:04:48,720 --> 00:04:50,400
MUTE, HANG UP, CAMERA

32
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:53,176
Have you done any internships?

33
00:04:53,200 --> 00:04:54,840
If you have, tell us about that.

34
00:04:54,920 --> 00:04:56,040
I have.

35
00:04:56,120 --> 00:04:57,640
While I was in college,

36
00:04:57,720 --> 00:05:00,600
I did some scenic area planning
projects with my classmates.

37
00:05:00,680 --> 00:05:03,560
We planned the event's itinerary,

38
00:05:03,640 --> 00:05:06,800
set up the stage, and worked
on posters and promotional texts.

39
00:05:06,880 --> 00:05:08,080
How big was the project?

40
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:10,440
There wasn't much funding,

41
00:05:10,520 --> 00:05:12,320
but we were very interested in it,

42
00:05:12,400 --> 00:05:15,160
so we joined with the goal of
gaining experience in mind...

43
00:05:15,240 --> 00:05:16,240
Okay.

44
00:05:16,760 --> 00:05:17,800
Next.

45
00:05:25,200 --> 00:05:27,160
Thank you, Shang Zhitao.

46
00:05:27,240 --> 00:05:29,520
That's all for your interview.

47
00:05:29,600 --> 00:05:30,976
Please go back and wait for our notice.

48
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:34,560
It wasn't a huge project, but
I gained a lot of experience.

49
00:05:34,640 --> 00:05:36,160
Maybe I can share it with you?

50
00:05:36,240 --> 00:05:39,240
No need. I need someone with
top-tier hands-on experience.

51
00:05:39,320 --> 00:05:41,400
You're not suitable. Next.

52
00:05:46,880 --> 00:05:47,920
Thank you.

53
00:05:58,880 --> 00:06:00,000
Luke.

54
00:06:00,080 --> 00:06:03,480
Is it possible for you to mind
your tone during interviews?

55
00:06:03,560 --> 00:06:05,400
Let them finish speaking, at least.

56
00:06:06,960 --> 00:06:08,040
Sure.

57
00:06:16,160 --> 00:06:17,320
Yao Bei.

58
00:06:17,400 --> 00:06:19,040
I failed the interview.

59
00:06:20,320 --> 00:06:21,320
What happened?

60
00:06:21,840 --> 00:06:24,200
Tao. I have to work overtime today.

61
00:06:24,280 --> 00:06:25,920
Let's meet up and talk another day, okay?

62
00:06:26,400 --> 00:06:30,560
It's okay. I just arrived
downstairs at the flat I'm renting.

63
00:06:30,640 --> 00:06:33,360
Once I find my unit, I'll settle in.

64
00:06:33,880 --> 00:06:36,640
Okay. Take your time
planning. Don't give up.

65
00:06:36,720 --> 00:06:39,760
It's normal to be rejected by
a renowned company like Lime.

66
00:06:39,840 --> 00:06:41,480
Getting in is like winning the lottery.

67
00:06:42,200 --> 00:06:43,320
I know.

68
00:06:43,400 --> 00:06:44,400
All right then.

69
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:55,680
TIANTONG DONGYUAN, SECTION 1

70
00:07:32,200 --> 00:07:33,200
Looking for someone?

71
00:07:34,040 --> 00:07:35,320
Sorry to bother you.

72
00:07:35,400 --> 00:07:37,440
I'm the new tenant.

73
00:07:37,520 --> 00:07:38,520
I contacted Zhang Lei.

74
00:07:41,640 --> 00:07:42,880
He's the landlord.

75
00:07:43,440 --> 00:07:44,520
Come in.

76
00:07:49,640 --> 00:07:50,720
Your room is here.

77
00:08:11,880 --> 00:08:15,360
It wasn't a huge project, but
I gained a lot of experience.

78
00:08:15,440 --> 00:08:17,800
-Maybe I can share them with you? -No need.

79
00:08:17,880 --> 00:08:20,080
You're not suitable. Next.

80
00:08:24,840 --> 00:08:26,360
He didn't even let me finish.

81
00:08:28,760 --> 00:08:29,760
It's okay.

82
00:08:30,680 --> 00:08:33,440
Man proposes, God disposes.

83
00:08:42,840 --> 00:08:44,880
Tao. Have you arrived in Beijing?

84
00:08:44,960 --> 00:08:46,160
Have you settled in?

85
00:08:46,240 --> 00:08:48,280
How are your unit and your housemate?

86
00:08:52,400 --> 00:08:54,120
I've arrived. Everything is good.

87
00:08:54,200 --> 00:08:55,400
Don't worry.

88
00:09:03,040 --> 00:09:04,056
FOLLOW-UP E-MAIL TO LIME ADVERTISING
REGARDING MY WORK EXPERIENCE

89
00:09:04,080 --> 00:09:05,136
I AM AN ADVERTISING STUDENT AT JINLING
UNIVERSITY OF FINANCE AND ECONOMICS

90
00:09:05,160 --> 00:09:06,080
I'VE FOLLOWED LIME'S OUTSTANDING
WORK IN BRANDING AND CREATIVE PLANNING

91
00:09:06,160 --> 00:09:07,920
A habitual thief, aren't you?

92
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:09,840
You keep stealing my detergent and shampoo.

93
00:09:09,920 --> 00:09:11,096
Don't you dare make things up.

94
00:09:11,120 --> 00:09:12,616
I could say you stole
my rings and earrings.

95
00:09:12,640 --> 00:09:13,800
Liar!

96
00:09:13,880 --> 00:09:16,000
My bracelet was on the sink counter.

97
00:09:16,080 --> 00:09:17,416
When I came back ten
minutes later, it was gone.

98
00:09:17,440 --> 00:09:19,496
Only you went to the toilet.
So you must be the thief.

99
00:09:19,520 --> 00:09:20,440
I did not steal it.

100
00:09:20,520 --> 00:09:21,816
If you slander us again,
I'll tear your mouth off.

101
00:09:21,840 --> 00:09:24,000
You lost something? Maybe
we should call the police.

102
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:26,800
Who are you? Why are you in my house?

103
00:09:26,880 --> 00:09:28,000
Right. Call the police.

104
00:09:28,080 --> 00:09:29,240
Now.

105
00:09:29,320 --> 00:09:30,696
Call the police. Where's your phone?

106
00:09:30,720 --> 00:09:32,136
What gives you the right
to say whatever you want?

107
00:09:32,160 --> 00:09:33,960
Look at how crazy you are.

108
00:09:34,040 --> 00:09:35,896
You always look miserable.
No wonder you're single.

109
00:09:35,920 --> 00:09:37,896
Your man lies in bed all
day. He doesn't go to work.

110
00:09:37,920 --> 00:09:39,040
"Honey, wash my socks."

111
00:09:39,120 --> 00:09:40,896
"Honey, wash my
underwear." "Wash it for me."

112
00:09:40,920 --> 00:09:42,680
Is it fun washing
someone's dirty underwear?

113
00:09:42,760 --> 00:09:45,400
-I do what I want. -Don't fight.

114
00:09:45,480 --> 00:09:46,880
-Don't hit her. -Move!

115
00:09:50,800 --> 00:09:51,640
Let her go!

116
00:09:51,720 --> 00:09:52,720
Come.

117
00:09:54,480 --> 00:09:55,840
Lock the door.

118
00:09:55,920 --> 00:09:57,280
-Open the door! -Open the door!

119
00:09:57,360 --> 00:09:58,680
You hit me. I'll call the police.

120
00:10:02,680 --> 00:10:04,240
-Open the door! -Hello, 110?

121
00:10:04,320 --> 00:10:05,320
I want to make a report.

122
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:19,240
Come in.

123
00:10:23,440 --> 00:10:25,520
The shortlist for this
graduate recruitment.

124
00:10:25,600 --> 00:10:26,600
Please sign it.

125
00:10:28,800 --> 00:10:31,200
GRADUATE RECRUITMENT SHORTLISTED
CANDIDATES, 5. SHANG ZHITAO

126
00:10:33,480 --> 00:10:34,560
Shang Zhitao?

127
00:10:36,080 --> 00:10:38,760
I thought I rejected
her during the interview.

128
00:10:39,360 --> 00:10:42,120
Yes. You did.

129
00:10:42,200 --> 00:10:43,360
But Luke,

130
00:10:43,440 --> 00:10:46,240
HR is all about diverse employment.

131
00:10:46,320 --> 00:10:48,800
I wasn't born to be an HRBP.

132
00:10:48,880 --> 00:10:50,880
We all went through a learning process.

133
00:10:51,520 --> 00:10:54,200
Our company has fielded
many competent individuals,

134
00:10:54,280 --> 00:10:56,920
but they're all too high up
and out of touch with reality.

135
00:10:57,560 --> 00:11:00,960
If this continues, the
team will have problems.

136
00:11:01,800 --> 00:11:04,680
But we can't recruit someone with
neither qualifications nor experience.

137
00:11:05,200 --> 00:11:06,400
Is she a relative of yours?

138
00:11:07,600 --> 00:11:09,640
Are you doubting my professionalism?

139
00:11:09,720 --> 00:11:11,480
You didn't even let her finish.

140
00:11:11,560 --> 00:11:13,320
After the interview,
she proactively sent me

141
00:11:13,400 --> 00:11:15,120
supplementary materials about her project.

142
00:11:15,200 --> 00:11:17,136
Her feedback in the
background check was the best.

143
00:11:17,160 --> 00:11:18,840
I have discussed this with headquarters.

144
00:11:18,920 --> 00:11:22,560
This time, I'll recruit some
down-to-earth fresh graduates.

145
00:11:23,080 --> 00:11:24,560
Consider this an experiment of mine.

146
00:11:25,160 --> 00:11:28,040
Besides, your Lumi keeps
asking me for more manpower.

147
00:11:28,120 --> 00:11:32,400
Can you please support my
endeavor and sign on the paper?

148
00:11:34,560 --> 00:11:35,720
Fine. This is a favor.

149
00:11:36,360 --> 00:11:38,120
Sure. I owe you one.

150
00:11:38,920 --> 00:11:40,960
The new recruits will report next Monday.

151
00:11:41,040 --> 00:11:42,760
Find some time and meet with them.

152
00:11:42,840 --> 00:11:44,840
You were at the training
seminar last year, right?

153
00:11:45,920 --> 00:11:48,720
I wasn't able to answer those questions.

154
00:11:49,320 --> 00:11:51,480
"Is office romance allowed?"

155
00:11:51,560 --> 00:11:55,520
Tracy, you're the one who decides
who gets to join our company.

156
00:11:55,600 --> 00:11:57,000
Please use your power wisely.

157
00:11:57,680 --> 00:11:58,720
Okay.

158
00:11:58,800 --> 00:12:00,080
I shall return and add

159
00:12:00,160 --> 00:12:02,040
"No asking about your
superior's personal life"

160
00:12:02,120 --> 00:12:05,360
and "No dating between
superiors and subordinates"

161
00:12:05,440 --> 00:12:08,760
to the new recruit's manual
in black and white. Happy?

162
00:12:08,840 --> 00:12:11,160
Congratulations. You've become
more and more professional.

163
00:12:11,960 --> 00:12:13,280
I shall go now.

164
00:12:20,160 --> 00:12:21,560
FARMHOUSE PORK

165
00:12:23,680 --> 00:12:26,320
So, you won't file a police report anymore?

166
00:12:28,040 --> 00:12:29,760
I've checked with Lei.

167
00:12:29,840 --> 00:12:33,000
He said they had already
mentioned moving out last month.

168
00:12:33,080 --> 00:12:37,440
Why else would they pack up so
quickly and leave while we were hiding?

169
00:12:39,280 --> 00:12:40,480
She stole my things. So be it.

170
00:12:40,560 --> 00:12:42,520
She can have them. I don't need them.

171
00:12:42,600 --> 00:12:43,600
Thank you for today.

172
00:12:43,640 --> 00:12:45,560
I am Sun Yu. What's your name?

173
00:12:46,240 --> 00:12:47,640
I am Shang Zhitao.

174
00:12:47,720 --> 00:12:49,280
Shang Zhitao.

175
00:12:52,040 --> 00:12:53,040
Thank you.

176
00:12:54,360 --> 00:12:57,600
I've never asked you this.
What do you do for work?

177
00:12:58,960 --> 00:12:59,960
Love business.

178
00:13:02,200 --> 00:13:06,760
I work in sales for a dating site.

179
00:13:06,840 --> 00:13:08,480
Isn't that love business?

180
00:13:11,720 --> 00:13:12,760
Where are you from?

181
00:13:13,360 --> 00:13:15,400
Me? I'm from Harbin.

182
00:13:15,480 --> 00:13:17,640
But I went to university in Nanjing.

183
00:13:19,360 --> 00:13:20,360
Nanjing?

184
00:13:22,680 --> 00:13:23,800
My ex is from Nanjing.

185
00:13:25,800 --> 00:13:27,840
I… Sorry.

186
00:13:27,920 --> 00:13:29,240
Don't be.

187
00:13:29,320 --> 00:13:31,000
He should be the one apologizing to me.

188
00:13:31,600 --> 00:13:34,400
He kept saying the feelings had faded.

189
00:13:34,920 --> 00:13:37,120
But I know he thinks I'm
not good enough for him.

190
00:13:38,200 --> 00:13:39,560
In Beijing,

191
00:13:40,400 --> 00:13:43,160
everyone has a price.

192
00:13:44,920 --> 00:13:46,520
They are waiting for the best offer.

193
00:13:48,640 --> 00:13:50,520
You're too good for him.

194
00:13:50,600 --> 00:13:51,640
He will surely regret it.

195
00:13:52,520 --> 00:13:53,880
Impossible.

196
00:13:55,400 --> 00:13:57,040
I won't let him hurt me again.

197
00:13:57,760 --> 00:13:58,920
You're right.

198
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:01,000
Don't let anyone hurt you again.

199
00:14:01,080 --> 00:14:02,120
Exactly.

200
00:14:03,280 --> 00:14:04,480
Screw love.

201
00:14:06,080 --> 00:14:07,560
I will be rich.

202
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:12,400
I won't let stupid romance weigh me down.

203
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:14,840
You have my support.

204
00:14:14,920 --> 00:14:16,560
I agree with you.

205
00:14:16,640 --> 00:14:20,400
When we're self-sufficient,
love will come after us.

206
00:14:21,200 --> 00:14:22,240
Good one.

207
00:14:23,640 --> 00:14:26,000
Meeting you is the beginning
of my good fortune. Thank you.

208
00:14:27,560 --> 00:14:28,400
Actually, I'm the lucky one.

209
00:14:28,480 --> 00:14:30,416
It's my first day in Beijing,
and someone is buying me a meal.

210
00:14:30,440 --> 00:14:32,240
You're so kind and brave.

211
00:14:32,800 --> 00:14:35,400
People will queue up to buy you a meal.

212
00:14:35,920 --> 00:14:37,680
Dig in. You haven't touched anything.

213
00:14:55,680 --> 00:14:58,920
OFFER LETTER BEIJING LIME ADVERTISING

214
00:15:03,960 --> 00:15:07,400
OFFER LETTER DEAR SHANG ZHITAO…

215
00:15:14,720 --> 00:15:17,600
Tao, can I come in?

216
00:15:20,080 --> 00:15:22,120
Thank you for today.

217
00:15:25,480 --> 00:15:26,920
What's the matter?

218
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:28,080
Why are you crying?

219
00:15:30,120 --> 00:15:31,240
What happened?

220
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:35,560
I… I found a job.

221
00:15:35,640 --> 00:15:37,360
You… You found a job?

222
00:15:37,960 --> 00:15:40,120
-Where? -Lime.

223
00:15:41,360 --> 00:15:42,560
Lime?

224
00:15:42,640 --> 00:15:43,640
Seriously?

225
00:15:43,680 --> 00:15:46,600
The Lime that made the
Olympic advertisements?

226
00:15:47,320 --> 00:15:49,560
Is this for real, Shang Zhitao?

227
00:15:52,280 --> 00:15:53,640
Beijing Lime.

228
00:15:54,280 --> 00:15:56,440
You're amazing!

229
00:15:59,320 --> 00:16:01,240
I was about to give this to you.

230
00:16:01,840 --> 00:16:03,480
You told me you were looking for a job.

231
00:16:03,560 --> 00:16:04,936
I got this lucky charm from Yonghe Temple.

232
00:16:04,960 --> 00:16:06,280
It will boost your career.

233
00:16:09,480 --> 00:16:10,960
Thank you, Sun Yu.

234
00:16:11,040 --> 00:16:14,120
-I really need it. -You are so amazing.

235
00:17:03,400 --> 00:17:04,560
Luke.

236
00:17:04,640 --> 00:17:05,800
I need to tell you something.

237
00:17:06,640 --> 00:17:07,720
An emergency?

238
00:17:07,800 --> 00:17:09,920
Qipai is very happy with
the annual plan we proposed.

239
00:17:10,760 --> 00:17:12,590
-So we sign now. -No.

240
00:17:12,680 --> 00:17:13,760
Something bad happened.

241
00:17:16,560 --> 00:17:19,480
They plan to use our design proposal
for their secondary line brand.

242
00:17:19,560 --> 00:17:22,070
And they want a discount. 30% discount.

243
00:17:22,160 --> 00:17:23,160
No.

244
00:17:24,240 --> 00:17:26,160
Their Asia Pacific regional manager said

245
00:17:26,240 --> 00:17:28,880
that the secondary line brand
would be their main push this year.

246
00:17:28,960 --> 00:17:29,960
If our design proposal

247
00:17:30,040 --> 00:17:32,920
can help them boost this year's sales,

248
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:35,320
next year, they'll let
us handle the marketing

249
00:17:35,400 --> 00:17:36,760
of all their brands under them.

250
00:17:36,840 --> 00:17:37,840
That's not good either.

251
00:17:39,960 --> 00:17:41,280
So we'll just lose the deal then.

252
00:17:41,920 --> 00:17:42,920
I'd rather lose them.

253
00:17:43,760 --> 00:17:46,520
They approved our proposal,
which means our ideas are good.

254
00:17:47,360 --> 00:17:49,976
They can choose to implement our
proposals on whichever product they want,

255
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:51,360
but we won't give them a discount.

256
00:17:52,040 --> 00:17:54,160
Our ideas are not for hawking,

257
00:17:54,240 --> 00:17:56,320
where people expect us to
give them a huge discount.

258
00:17:56,640 --> 00:17:59,680
Okay. I'll confirm the
quotation with Finance.

259
00:18:02,640 --> 00:18:03,880
You look dashing today.

260
00:18:24,640 --> 00:18:26,000
Handle the file.

261
00:18:27,680 --> 00:18:29,400
-Morning, Luke. -Morning, Luke.

262
00:18:31,800 --> 00:18:33,040
So, he is Luke.

263
00:18:37,680 --> 00:18:38,760
Morning, Luke.

264
00:18:43,480 --> 00:18:44,480
Morning.

265
00:18:56,760 --> 00:18:57,960
Luke.

266
00:18:58,920 --> 00:19:00,600
I'm the new recruit, Shang Zhitao.

267
00:19:00,680 --> 00:19:02,200
Thank you for recruiting me.

268
00:19:03,440 --> 00:19:05,680
No need to thank me. I did not recruit you.

269
00:19:06,560 --> 00:19:08,480
In my eyes, you're not good enough.

270
00:19:11,600 --> 00:19:13,560
Then, I shall thank
Lime for this opportunity.

271
00:19:13,640 --> 00:19:14,760
I'll work hard.

272
00:19:16,960 --> 00:19:18,880
I hope you'll pass the probation,

273
00:19:19,440 --> 00:19:21,920
instead of just using us to
polish your resume before leaving.

274
00:19:26,200 --> 00:19:29,320
I am incredibly lucky and
honored to be able to work

275
00:19:29,400 --> 00:19:31,680
in this world-class advertising company.

276
00:19:31,760 --> 00:19:33,400
I will do my best to stay here.

277
00:19:38,120 --> 00:19:39,960
New hire? You know her?

278
00:19:41,760 --> 00:19:44,000
Why would I know a nobody
from the labor market?

279
00:19:47,640 --> 00:19:49,560
Who got him so upset
this early in the morning?

280
00:19:50,920 --> 00:19:52,240
We spoiled him, didn't we?

281
00:19:56,840 --> 00:19:57,960
Tracy.

282
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:07,000
Welcome to Lime China.

283
00:20:07,080 --> 00:20:09,280
I am Liang Xin, the HR manager.

284
00:20:09,360 --> 00:20:11,816
In our company culture, we address
each other by our English names.

285
00:20:11,840 --> 00:20:13,200
So, please call me Tracy.

286
00:20:13,800 --> 00:20:17,520
Allow me to brief you and show you around.

287
00:20:18,200 --> 00:20:19,400
Come with me.

288
00:20:21,680 --> 00:20:24,800
What you're seeing now is an
introduction to our company.

289
00:20:25,600 --> 00:20:27,320
This is the Creative Division.

290
00:20:27,400 --> 00:20:28,576
Are you sure they want
to change it this way?

291
00:20:28,600 --> 00:20:30,200
It's the same as our first draft.

292
00:20:33,360 --> 00:20:34,200
START

293
00:20:34,280 --> 00:20:35,880
This is the Business Division.

294
00:20:35,960 --> 00:20:38,160
The busiest division in our company.

295
00:20:40,080 --> 00:20:42,576
I'll notify the supplier about
the client's request immediately

296
00:20:42,600 --> 00:20:43,960
so that they can find a new venue.

297
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:45,776
The Commerce Division. We have a
business negotiation this afternoon.

298
00:20:45,800 --> 00:20:47,280
Get the collaboration proposal ready.

299
00:20:47,320 --> 00:20:48,040
Let's begin.

300
00:20:48,120 --> 00:20:49,320
This is the pantry.

301
00:20:49,400 --> 00:20:51,160
There's a lounge in the back.

302
00:20:51,680 --> 00:20:52,800
This is the public space.

303
00:20:52,880 --> 00:20:54,400
You can use it whenever you want.

304
00:20:54,480 --> 00:20:55,576
Recap of the situation. Last month…

305
00:20:55,600 --> 00:20:57,296
There are several
restaurants near the office.

306
00:20:57,320 --> 00:20:59,096
When you show your Lime work
badge, you'll get a 20% discount.

307
00:20:59,120 --> 00:21:01,920
You'll find the details
in the employee manual.

308
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:03,776
Your probation period
will last for three months,

309
00:21:03,800 --> 00:21:05,240
and you'll rotate through divisions.

310
00:21:05,320 --> 00:21:07,760
Once you've decided to work
in a particular division,

311
00:21:07,840 --> 00:21:09,840
you may end the rotational shift.

312
00:21:09,920 --> 00:21:11,480
Have I made myself clear?

313
00:21:11,560 --> 00:21:12,480
Yes.

314
00:21:12,560 --> 00:21:15,440
Your first position is
in Business Division One.

315
00:21:15,520 --> 00:21:17,360
You will work under…

316
00:21:17,440 --> 00:21:18,360
Lumi.

317
00:21:18,440 --> 00:21:19,640
Tracy.

318
00:21:22,360 --> 00:21:23,360
Allow me to introduce.

319
00:21:23,960 --> 00:21:25,200
Lumi, your mentor.

320
00:21:25,280 --> 00:21:26,560
You'll be working for her.

321
00:21:27,360 --> 00:21:29,840
-Hi, madam. -Wow.

322
00:21:29,920 --> 00:21:31,960
Are fresh graduates this nerdy nowadays?

323
00:21:32,040 --> 00:21:35,600
Perhaps you can show her the
true colors of corporate life.

324
00:21:35,680 --> 00:21:37,480
Please be nice to kids.

325
00:21:38,160 --> 00:21:39,320
Don't be like Luke.

326
00:21:40,040 --> 00:21:41,160
Tracy.

327
00:21:41,240 --> 00:21:44,400
Come on. I have no filter.

328
00:21:44,480 --> 00:21:47,120
But work is work. Don't
treat it like a joking matter.

329
00:21:47,200 --> 00:21:48,320
Worry not, madam.

330
00:21:48,400 --> 00:21:49,600
I'll work hard.

331
00:21:49,680 --> 00:21:50,840
All right.

332
00:21:50,920 --> 00:21:52,160
She'll work for me now.

333
00:21:52,240 --> 00:21:54,240
Come. Let me show you your desk.

334
00:21:55,000 --> 00:21:56,000
Don't worry.

335
00:21:57,880 --> 00:21:59,400
You'll sit here.

336
00:21:59,480 --> 00:22:00,800
Ms. Lumi.

337
00:22:00,880 --> 00:22:03,400
I am Shang Zhitao. Or Flora.

338
00:22:04,560 --> 00:22:06,360
No need to add "miss".

339
00:22:06,440 --> 00:22:08,160
Just call me Lumi.

340
00:22:08,240 --> 00:22:10,000
My English and Chinese names are both Lumi.

341
00:22:11,840 --> 00:22:14,120
That row there is the
offices of all the bigwigs.

342
00:22:14,760 --> 00:22:18,120
And that one in particular, avoid it.

343
00:22:20,320 --> 00:22:21,640
Mr. Luan's office?

344
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:25,080
You're smart.

345
00:22:25,720 --> 00:22:28,360
At work, just call him Luke.

346
00:22:28,440 --> 00:22:30,840
All right. I'll send
you some documents later.

347
00:22:30,920 --> 00:22:32,840
Familiarize yourself with our projects,

348
00:22:32,920 --> 00:22:34,560
and wait for my call.

349
00:22:35,440 --> 00:22:37,880
Oh. Report yourself to Luke first.

350
00:22:37,960 --> 00:22:41,520
While you do that, conduct
the interview as well.

351
00:22:41,600 --> 00:22:42,760
Compile your questions now.

352
00:22:42,840 --> 00:22:44,520
Interview?

353
00:22:44,600 --> 00:22:46,280
I will interview Luke?

354
00:22:46,360 --> 00:22:49,720
It is our tradition that the
new hire will interview the boss.

355
00:22:50,400 --> 00:22:52,240
Book an appointment with him today.

356
00:23:14,400 --> 00:23:15,640
Lumi.

357
00:23:16,240 --> 00:23:18,280
-You startled me. -Sorry.

358
00:23:18,840 --> 00:23:23,520
I have a question. Must
I do the interview today?

359
00:23:26,240 --> 00:23:27,240
You're afraid of him?

360
00:23:28,840 --> 00:23:31,440
I heard he's quite strict.

361
00:23:31,520 --> 00:23:33,000
I'm just a bit worried.

362
00:23:35,560 --> 00:23:37,800
Creative people can be cranky.

363
00:23:37,880 --> 00:23:41,080
He's blunt, but he can be reasoned with.

364
00:23:41,160 --> 00:23:42,760
He won't devour you. Careful.

365
00:23:43,680 --> 00:23:45,880
He has already vented his anger today.

366
00:23:47,520 --> 00:23:49,816
He yelled at three people until
they cried at the morning meeting,

367
00:23:49,840 --> 00:23:51,440
so he probably won't yell again.

368
00:23:52,000 --> 00:23:55,400
What can I do to get along with
him if I don't want to be yelled at?

369
00:23:58,120 --> 00:23:59,560
Get along with him?

370
00:24:01,040 --> 00:24:02,520
Do you want to date him or something?

371
00:24:05,360 --> 00:24:06,800
You're blushing.

372
00:24:08,080 --> 00:24:09,080
I have one tip for you.

373
00:24:09,600 --> 00:24:12,440
At work, the more prideful your boss is,

374
00:24:12,520 --> 00:24:14,160
the more thick-skinned you have to be.

375
00:24:15,360 --> 00:24:16,400
Thick-skinned?

376
00:24:17,600 --> 00:24:18,800
Good luck.

377
00:24:46,200 --> 00:24:47,400
Come in.

378
00:24:55,000 --> 00:24:56,240
Hi, Luke.

379
00:24:56,320 --> 00:24:58,920
I am Shang Zhitao, the new
hire in Business Division One.

380
00:24:59,000 --> 00:25:00,040
You can call me Flora.

381
00:25:00,120 --> 00:25:01,640
Do you have time now?

382
00:25:01,720 --> 00:25:03,480
I have some questions for you.

383
00:25:04,320 --> 00:25:05,600
Is it urgent?

384
00:25:05,680 --> 00:25:07,120
Not really.

385
00:25:09,440 --> 00:25:10,520
Not urgent?

386
00:25:10,600 --> 00:25:11,600
Then, wait here.

387
00:25:43,640 --> 00:25:45,320
She doesn't hide a thing.

388
00:25:45,400 --> 00:25:47,920
You won't find someone
so guileless in Lime.

389
00:26:04,160 --> 00:26:05,600
Hello.

390
00:26:06,560 --> 00:26:07,720
Luan Nian.

391
00:26:07,800 --> 00:26:09,240
I don't want to break up.

392
00:26:09,320 --> 00:26:10,440
Can we…

393
00:26:10,520 --> 00:26:12,240
Can we sit down and talk things through?

394
00:26:12,320 --> 00:26:13,976
- Do not call me with a new number again.
- Luan Nian!

395
00:26:14,000 --> 00:26:15,000
Luan...

396
00:26:19,880 --> 00:26:20,960
Luke.

397
00:26:22,240 --> 00:26:23,240
Are you free now?

398
00:26:25,000 --> 00:26:26,040
You said it wasn't urgent.

399
00:26:27,480 --> 00:26:29,360
I assumed your time wasn't worth much,

400
00:26:29,440 --> 00:26:30,880
so your work could be deprioritized.

401
00:26:34,080 --> 00:26:35,240
I understand now.

402
00:26:35,320 --> 00:26:37,640
I will be direct about my
needs with you from now on.

403
00:26:37,720 --> 00:26:39,360
Thank you for the lesson.

404
00:26:39,440 --> 00:26:41,200
I did not teach you
anything. You may leave.

405
00:26:43,680 --> 00:26:46,240
Luke, according to the company's policy,

406
00:26:46,320 --> 00:26:48,480
you need to work with me as a new hire

407
00:26:48,560 --> 00:26:49,960
to have the interview.

408
00:26:50,040 --> 00:26:53,280
If you are not free today,
I'll follow up tomorrow.

409
00:26:53,360 --> 00:26:54,560
Just do it now.

410
00:26:56,920 --> 00:26:57,920
Sure.

411
00:27:00,880 --> 00:27:03,000
Why did you join Lime?

412
00:27:03,080 --> 00:27:04,080
The pay is great.

413
00:27:07,720 --> 00:27:08,720
The pay is great.

414
00:27:09,760 --> 00:27:13,040
-Do you like your job? -No.

415
00:27:14,440 --> 00:27:16,920
Then, why are you staying?

416
00:27:19,040 --> 00:27:20,080
To make money and splurge.

417
00:27:23,280 --> 00:27:24,280
Okay.

418
00:27:24,880 --> 00:27:28,920
Allow me to share the projects I will be
joining in the future with you one by one.

419
00:27:29,000 --> 00:27:32,120
- I look forward to your further guidance.
- I will not guide you.

420
00:27:32,200 --> 00:27:33,600
You can just ask Lumi for anything.

421
00:27:34,160 --> 00:27:35,280
But I hope you can...

422
00:27:35,360 --> 00:27:37,320
Can you differentiate ROI and CVR?

423
00:27:37,400 --> 00:27:39,560
Can you use SWOT analysis
to market a product?

424
00:27:39,640 --> 00:27:42,520
Can you differentiate
between advertising channels?

425
00:27:43,840 --> 00:27:45,400
Sorry. Can you repeat?

426
00:27:45,480 --> 00:27:47,920
I'll take them down and try
to get back to you by tomorrow.

427
00:27:48,000 --> 00:27:49,920
If you really want a
piece of advice from me,

428
00:27:50,000 --> 00:27:52,040
it'll be to find a new
job as soon as possible.

429
00:27:52,560 --> 00:27:53,560
You're not fit for Lime.

430
00:28:01,360 --> 00:28:02,920
Why do you think

431
00:28:04,040 --> 00:28:05,040
I'm not a good fit?

432
00:28:11,160 --> 00:28:13,040
Academics-wise, you're average.

433
00:28:13,640 --> 00:28:15,720
Background-wise, you have no connections.

434
00:28:15,800 --> 00:28:18,696
Experience-wise, you have no experience
with large-scale advertising projects.

435
00:28:18,720 --> 00:28:20,200
What do you bring to the table?

436
00:28:20,800 --> 00:28:24,160
Why should I waste my time on
someone who will be replaced soon?

437
00:28:28,040 --> 00:28:29,360
I have been accepted into Lime.

438
00:28:29,440 --> 00:28:31,680
That means I must have some value.

439
00:28:32,320 --> 00:28:34,120
I will do my best to keep up with you.

440
00:28:34,200 --> 00:28:35,320
I won't waste your time.

441
00:28:35,400 --> 00:28:37,080
You're wasting everyone's time.

442
00:28:37,680 --> 00:28:39,056
You can't even understand what I'm saying.

443
00:28:39,080 --> 00:28:40,400
I don't deal with idiots.

444
00:28:41,960 --> 00:28:43,856
What kind of person do
you like to deal with then?

445
00:28:43,880 --> 00:28:45,880
-I can... -I deal with jerks

446
00:28:45,960 --> 00:28:47,800
ike me. Can you do that?

447
00:28:53,200 --> 00:28:54,200
Okay.

448
00:28:55,080 --> 00:28:56,160
Duly noted.

449
00:28:56,240 --> 00:28:57,240
Thank you.

450
00:28:58,520 --> 00:28:59,520
I will go now.

451
00:29:10,880 --> 00:29:12,960
Sorry. I… I'll buy a new one.

452
00:29:15,680 --> 00:29:18,000
You can't afford it. Get out.

453
00:29:20,880 --> 00:29:22,080
Get out now.

454
00:29:35,240 --> 00:29:37,640
SHANG ZHITAO

455
00:29:44,360 --> 00:29:46,960
You must be the new intern.

456
00:29:48,000 --> 00:29:49,080
No, I'm not.

457
00:29:49,160 --> 00:29:51,400
I'm a full-time employee.

458
00:29:51,480 --> 00:29:53,240
Today is my first day.

459
00:29:53,320 --> 00:29:55,080
I am Shang Zhitao, Flora.

460
00:29:55,680 --> 00:29:56,680
Hi, I'm Jack.

461
00:29:57,320 --> 00:29:59,400
Are you free? Can you
get me a cup of coffee?

462
00:30:02,160 --> 00:30:03,160
Sure.

463
00:30:03,840 --> 00:30:04,840
Thank you.

464
00:30:04,920 --> 00:30:06,520
Does anyone else want coffee?

465
00:30:09,160 --> 00:30:10,480
You love making coffee that much?

466
00:30:11,320 --> 00:30:13,080
Why don't you make
everyone a cup of coffee?

467
00:30:13,600 --> 00:30:15,160
Lumi. Conference Room One.

468
00:30:15,240 --> 00:30:17,400
-Meeting in ten minutes. -Noted.

469
00:30:18,240 --> 00:30:19,240
Iced Americano.

470
00:30:24,320 --> 00:30:28,080
Flora, from now on in this company,
ask me before you do anything.

471
00:30:28,160 --> 00:30:30,800
I am your mentor. I'll tell you what to do.

472
00:30:30,880 --> 00:30:32,000
Do you hear me?

473
00:30:33,200 --> 00:30:34,640
-Yes. -Don't be too meek.

474
00:30:34,720 --> 00:30:38,120
In this office, people will bully the weak.

475
00:30:38,200 --> 00:30:40,096
The more sheepish you are, the
more they take advantage of you.

476
00:30:40,120 --> 00:30:41,696
They will then ask you
to do all the hard labor.

477
00:30:41,720 --> 00:30:42,880
You won't be able to take it.

478
00:30:44,880 --> 00:30:46,200
Have you conducted the interview?

479
00:30:47,040 --> 00:30:48,040
Yes.

480
00:30:48,760 --> 00:30:49,920
Lumi.

481
00:30:50,000 --> 00:30:53,680
Well, is the typewriter in
Luke's office very expensive?

482
00:30:53,760 --> 00:30:57,400
I ran into it just now, and
he said I could never afford it.

483
00:30:57,920 --> 00:30:59,160
You are quite something.

484
00:30:59,680 --> 00:31:00,880
He loves that thing.

485
00:31:00,960 --> 00:31:03,320
I'm not sure how expensive it is.

486
00:31:04,440 --> 00:31:05,880
Meeting first. We'll talk after.

487
00:31:19,000 --> 00:31:22,200
LEISURE WORK AREA

488
00:31:32,520 --> 00:31:33,696
MINUTES OF MANAGEMENT INTERVIEWS

489
00:31:33,720 --> 00:31:34,720
SEND

490
00:31:46,440 --> 00:31:48,000
Q&A OF THE INTERVIEW

491
00:31:48,080 --> 00:31:49,176
QUESTIONING OF PERSONAL
CAPABILITIES AND FUTURE PROJECTS

492
00:31:49,200 --> 00:31:52,400
THE LEADER REPEATEDLY USED NEGATIVE AND
AGGRESSIVE LANGUAGE DURING THE INTERVIEW

493
00:31:59,120 --> 00:31:59,960
Hello?

494
00:32:00,040 --> 00:32:03,160
You told the new hire
that you worked to splurge?

495
00:32:03,240 --> 00:32:04,080
TO MAKE MONEY AND SPLURGE

496
00:32:04,160 --> 00:32:05,736
Why are you staying if
you don't like the job?

497
00:32:05,760 --> 00:32:07,040
To make money and splurge.

498
00:32:08,640 --> 00:32:09,920
What else?

499
00:32:10,000 --> 00:32:11,256
And you told her to find a new job.

500
00:32:11,280 --> 00:32:12,560
I ADVISE YOU TO GET A NEW JOB

501
00:32:12,640 --> 00:32:13,800
You're not fit for Lime.

502
00:32:14,600 --> 00:32:15,600
Is that a problem?

503
00:32:15,680 --> 00:32:17,160
And you want her to be a jerk?

504
00:32:17,920 --> 00:32:19,336
What kind of person do
you like to deal with then?

505
00:32:19,360 --> 00:32:21,280
I deal with jerks.

506
00:32:21,880 --> 00:32:22,880
Is that a problem?

507
00:32:23,320 --> 00:32:26,216
The advertisement industry needs us
to be bold and yet unfazed by anything.

508
00:32:26,240 --> 00:32:28,616
Are you aware that your next
promotion is around the corner?

509
00:32:28,640 --> 00:32:31,520
Does that have anything
to do with the interview?

510
00:32:31,600 --> 00:32:33,280
Not directly,

511
00:32:33,360 --> 00:32:35,960
but you must respect our
diversity employment policy.

512
00:32:36,040 --> 00:32:37,400
I respect that,

513
00:32:37,480 --> 00:32:39,400
but it has nothing to
do with my opinion of her.

514
00:32:39,480 --> 00:32:40,680
What's so bad about her?

515
00:32:40,760 --> 00:32:43,040
It's her first day at work.

516
00:32:43,120 --> 00:32:44,760
If you weren't my junior,

517
00:32:44,840 --> 00:32:47,720
I would've reported you to the
board and asked them to fire you.

518
00:32:48,240 --> 00:32:49,440
Go ahead.

519
00:33:03,800 --> 00:33:05,200
She's indeed an idiot.

520
00:33:15,920 --> 00:33:19,360
JINGHUANANJIE STATION
OPERATION HOURS: 05:30-22:00

521
00:33:22,400 --> 00:33:24,720
23:08, JUNE 21, THURSDAY

522
00:33:28,160 --> 00:33:31,640
LOWER CARBON, GREENER LIVING

523
00:33:34,200 --> 00:33:36,240
If you really want a
piece of advice from me,

524
00:33:36,320 --> 00:33:38,200
it'll be to find a new
job as soon as possible.

525
00:33:39,000 --> 00:33:40,000
You're not fit for Lime.

526
00:33:43,680 --> 00:33:45,120
I'm staying, regardless.

527
00:33:53,880 --> 00:33:55,640
Hang on. Where are you heading?

528
00:33:55,720 --> 00:33:56,640
I have to hand over the shift soon.

529
00:33:56,720 --> 00:33:58,616
I can't give you a ride if
we're not going the same way.

530
00:33:58,640 --> 00:34:00,400
Tiantongyuan. Is that okay?

531
00:34:00,480 --> 00:34:02,400
It's too far. Sorry. I
don't have enough petrol.

532
00:34:15,760 --> 00:34:17,600
Want a ride? Where to?

533
00:34:17,670 --> 00:34:20,560
- I… I'm going to Tiantongyuan.
- One hundred and twenty yuan.

534
00:34:21,440 --> 00:34:22,440
That's too expensive.

535
00:34:22,480 --> 00:34:23,880
Expensive?

536
00:34:23,960 --> 00:34:25,080
Do you know what time it is?

537
00:34:25,120 --> 00:34:26,160
No one goes there anymore.

538
00:34:26,230 --> 00:34:27,520
Hop in. Let's go.

539
00:34:39,190 --> 00:34:40,280
Hop in.

540
00:34:43,800 --> 00:34:46,080
No, thanks. I found a cab.

541
00:34:46,150 --> 00:34:48,040
It's illegal to stop here.

542
00:35:03,360 --> 00:35:05,880
He's driving a Mercedes-Benz
and yet he's stealing my business.

543
00:35:08,080 --> 00:35:10,000
JING Z 59Q00

544
00:35:13,200 --> 00:35:14,440
Fasten your seat belt.

545
00:35:28,040 --> 00:35:29,080
Thanks, Luke.

546
00:35:30,520 --> 00:35:32,200
You may drop me off in front.

547
00:35:32,800 --> 00:35:34,040
I'll hail a cab back.

548
00:35:35,840 --> 00:35:38,040
Drop you off so that you
can get into another scam cab?

549
00:35:39,000 --> 00:35:41,920
There was a piece of chewing gum
on that scammer's license plate.

550
00:35:42,000 --> 00:35:43,000
The O on it became a Q.

551
00:35:49,760 --> 00:35:51,520
Stop looking at it. Where do you stay?

552
00:35:54,520 --> 00:35:55,520
Luke.

553
00:35:55,600 --> 00:35:57,800
I live quite far away.

554
00:35:58,400 --> 00:35:59,560
My home is in Tiantongyuan.

555
00:35:59,640 --> 00:36:00,760
I don't want to trouble you.

556
00:36:03,040 --> 00:36:04,200
You don't want to trouble me?

557
00:36:04,560 --> 00:36:06,880
You wrote in the interview
that I asked you to quit.

558
00:36:08,720 --> 00:36:11,480
HR said I couldn't make
things up for the interview,

559
00:36:11,560 --> 00:36:13,760
so I was being honest.

560
00:36:17,600 --> 00:36:19,200
You can be quite crafty.

561
00:36:19,720 --> 00:36:20,720
Just a bit, though.

562
00:36:37,960 --> 00:36:40,120
TIANTONG DONGYUAN

563
00:36:40,200 --> 00:36:42,280
-Is this the place? -Yes, it's here.

564
00:36:42,360 --> 00:36:44,360
-Get out. -Thanks.

565
00:36:51,920 --> 00:36:53,200
Luke.

566
00:36:53,720 --> 00:36:55,640
I am not challenging your authority.

567
00:36:55,720 --> 00:36:58,320
I have noted down
everything you said today.

568
00:37:01,800 --> 00:37:02,800
You noted it down?

569
00:37:04,120 --> 00:37:06,920
Are you using it against me
immediately and being a jerk

570
00:37:07,000 --> 00:37:08,480
or to get back at me?

571
00:37:10,920 --> 00:37:15,160
No. HR told me to write
everything down truthfully.

572
00:37:16,200 --> 00:37:18,481
Being only truthful won't
make you last in this industry.

573
00:37:18,880 --> 00:37:19,760
You're not fit for Lime.

574
00:37:19,840 --> 00:37:20,880
That's my real advice.

575
00:37:21,640 --> 00:37:22,640
Go home now.

576
00:37:26,720 --> 00:37:27,840
You…

577
00:37:28,360 --> 00:37:30,080
Why do you hate me so much?

578
00:37:31,200 --> 00:37:33,600
Is it because I ruined your typewriter?

579
00:37:33,680 --> 00:37:35,120
I can compensate you.

580
00:37:35,200 --> 00:37:37,280
Can I pay you back through
monthly installments?

581
00:37:37,960 --> 00:37:39,200
It has nothing to do with it.

582
00:37:39,720 --> 00:37:41,160
And you don't need to compensate me.

583
00:37:43,880 --> 00:37:45,080
I'm so sorry.

584
00:37:48,160 --> 00:37:49,160
I won't quit.

585
00:37:49,240 --> 00:37:50,680
Thank you for the lift.

586
00:37:59,120 --> 00:38:01,960
She looks meek, as if anyone can bully her.

587
00:38:02,480 --> 00:38:04,520
But when she's mad, she will fight back.

588
00:38:05,520 --> 00:38:06,560
Just a little, that's all.

589
00:39:21,400 --> 00:39:23,440
Sun Yu. Sun Yu.

590
00:39:25,440 --> 00:39:26,440
Sun Yu!

591
00:39:56,080 --> 00:39:57,280
Help!

592
00:40:33,280 --> 00:40:34,680
LOWER CARBON, GREENER LIVING

593
00:40:42,040 --> 00:40:45,200
I am incredibly lucky and
honored to be able to work

594
00:40:45,280 --> 00:40:47,560
in this world-class advertising company.

595
00:40:47,640 --> 00:40:49,560
I will do my best to stay here.

596
00:41:01,040 --> 00:41:02,080
Hop in.

